# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output.
#
# The bare root is not a language, so it goes to the default one, which is
# ENGLISH from 2026-08-02 (DESIGN-PLAN section 37). Astro's own
# static redirect emits an index.html carrying a meta refresh, which works but
# answers 200 and costs the reader a round trip. Cloudflare applies redirects
# before static assets, so this turns the same hop into a real 301. The Astro
# page stays underneath as a fallback and is what the dev server uses.
#
# This is a path redirect, not language detection: nothing here reads
# Accept-Language, and the switch stays visible on every page.
/  /en  301

# The pieces are Creature, the owner's own word for them (DESIGN-PLAN section
# 22), so /pieces/ became /creature/ on 2026-08-02. Nothing had been shared and
# the site is noindexed, so nothing is known to break; these exist because a URL
# that once resolved should not start answering 404, and they cost nothing.
# The archive became a GALLERY on 2026-08-03 (DESIGN-PLAN section 18): it holds
# the brand's imagery as a sequence, not a dated record, so the label and the
# path now say the same thing.
/it/archive  /it/gallery  301
/en/archive  /en/gallery  301

/it/pieces/*  /it/creature/:splat  301
/en/pieces/*  /en/creature/:splat  301
